  title: 'Weather in Singapore (Present Day) '
  info: "Singapore has a tropical climate with hot and humid weather year-round.
    Temperatures range from 25\xB0C to 32\xB0C, with frequent rainfall due to monsoon
    seasons. Thunderstorms are common, especially in the afternoons. The high humidity,
    often exceeding 80%, can make the heat feel more intense. While there are no
    distinct seasons, the wettest months are from November to January, while the
    driest are from June to August. Singapore\u2019s urban design incorporates air-conditioned
    spaces and greenery to help residents cope with the heat.  "
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5115cf0708ef747f380fc999d1132c61, type: 3}
